Here's a Java solution to determine if a given integer `n` is a power of three without using loops or recursion:

```java
public class PowerOfThreeChecker {

    public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        // Check if n is less than 1 because no power of 3 is less than 1
        if (n < 1) {
            return false;
        }

        // Check if n is exactly 1, which is a power of 3
        if (n == 1) {
            return true;
        }

        // Check if n is divisible by 3
        if (n % 3 != 0) {
            return false;
        }

        // Continue dividing by 3 until n is no longer divisible
        while (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        }

        // If n is reduced to 1, it's a power of 3; otherwise, it's not
        return n == 1;
    }

    public static void main

